  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 108 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nNot much change going into the holiday weekend. Upper level\nridging will continue to dominate our weather through the 4th of\nJuly. Highs from Thursday through Saturday will be in the mid 90s\nto near 102 degrees, with mostly sunny skies and breezy southerly\nwinds persisting. We continue to look at the potential for a \npattern change for the beginning of next week. The upper level \nridge over the southeast U.S. is forecast to weaken, with an upper\nlevel low developing over south Texas. The result will be the \npossibility of scattered showers and storms along with a bit \ncooler temperatures. Still not expecting anything significant in \nterms of rainfall, but any relief we can get will be welcome.",
